# CFG_CONFIG: the CONFIG_SITE (ICAP, STARTUP, BSCAN, DNA_PORT, ...). A tile
# type the reference never fuzzed; its window is in tilegrid.windows.
# Solved from designs/kv260_cfg_char: one primitive per specimen against a
# baseline with none, bits relative to the whole-frame window (frame-ECC
# halfwords masked).
#
# ICAP_TOP.IN_USE: Vivado's ICAPE3 (placed on ICAP_TOP) sets exactly these.
# Board-verified: kv260_icap_idcode reads the IDCODE with them and all-zero
# with only the other config-column bit Vivado sets (row 3, word 47).
CFG_CONFIG.ICAP_TOP.IN_USE add-feature 00_1892 01_1891 01_1892
# The same for an ICAPE3 placed (BEL property) on ICAP_BOT. ICAP_AUTO_SWITCH
# changes nothing in the frames.
CFG_CONFIG.ICAP_BOT.IN_USE add-feature 00_1893 00_1894 01_1893

# DNA_PORTE2 and BSCANE2 (JTAG_CHAIN 1-4, one bel each): one specimen each,
# the only CFG_CONFIG bits set against the baseline.
CFG_CONFIG.DNA_PORT.IN_USE add-feature 00_1890 00_1891 01_1890
CFG_CONFIG.BSCAN1.IN_USE add-feature 01_1909
CFG_CONFIG.BSCAN2.IN_USE add-feature 00_1910
CFG_CONFIG.BSCAN3.IN_USE add-feature 01_1910
CFG_CONFIG.BSCAN4.IN_USE add-feature 00_1911

# STARTUPE3: IN_USE with every pin tied to its inactive level; PROG_USR="TRUE"
# adds three more. (Driving USRCCLKO or USRDONEO from logic adds
# 00_1901 01_1900 01_1901 in both specimens alike, so what those bits mean is
# not separated yet, and nextpnr does not write them.)
CFG_CONFIG.STARTUP.IN_USE add-feature 00_1908 00_1909 01_1908
CFG_CONFIG.STARTUP.PROG_USR add-feature 00_1902 00_1903 01_1902

# FRAME_ECCE4, EFUSE_USR and USR_ACCESSE2 set no CFG_CONFIG bits (their
# specimens match the baseline); only their routing is configured. The
# USR_ACCESS value lives in the bitstream's AXSS register, not in frames.
